WEBVTT

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.170
I hope Mizushima-senpai will be back soon.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.610
I want to hear about her date!

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.130
S-S-Suzu, don't be so nervous!

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.080
J-J-Just try to wait calmly!

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:15.520
Congratulations on Your Six Month 
Anniversary, Mizushima-senpai

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.530
<i>You</i> need to calm down.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:18.780
It's your own fault if you're let down 
because your hopes were too high.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.620
Anyway, Sayo sure is taking a long time.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.800
Passions reignite after six months apart.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.740
Their hands gently overlap 
as they move closer, and...

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.960
<b>Smooch</b>

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:30.960
and then...

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.870
You're way too excited.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.560
It's a guy and a girl we're talking about.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.600
No matter what we pry out of her, 
let's try not to act surprised.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.830
Hey.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:44.390
Congratulations on Your 
Six Month Anniversary

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.170
What have you been doing, Sayo?

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.060
You're late.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.710
We're tired of waiting.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:50.580
So? So?

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:51.570
How was it?

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.830
The school found out about my boyfriend.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.490
So, I'm quitting the student council.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:57.630
Huh?

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.990
What did you say?

00:00:59.220 --> 00:00:59.880
Huh?

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:00.690
Huh?

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.000
<i>What?!</i>

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.480
Wait, what's going on?

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:40.160
<b>That Smile...</b>

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:40.010
Ichikawa had photographic evidence.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:40.830
What?

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.850
She's so dimwitted, I underestimated her.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.440
If she managed to sneak up 
on me without me noticing,

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.380
maybe her boorishness was just an act.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.310
This isn't the time to be impressed!

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:56.650
Anyway, make sure you tell her you 
didn't know about my boyfriend.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.000
Are you serious?

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.180
You're going to take the fall for this alone?

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.070
Sacrificing yourself like that is just—

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.700
It's... unforgivable. Yes.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.620
It was my choice, and my mistake, 
to have a boyfriend and go on a date with him.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.620
Now that she has proof, 
there's no point in denying it.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.630
It would be stupid to let this 
blow up into a big deal.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.800
In other words, this isn't like 
what happened to you, Kurahashi.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.470
See you.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.360
Hey, wait!

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.440
Sayo!

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.580
Senpai, do you...

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.430
Mizushima-senpai, do you want 
to quit the student council?

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.030
Yeah. I've had enough.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:44.450
Later.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.300
No...

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.110
Enomoto-senpai?

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:03.970
This is not right!

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.520
Hey!

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.290
Suzu!

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:13.520
Hey, Suzu!

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:16.130
Damn it, what do they think they're doing?

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.290
Maki, what should we do?

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:25.400
Maki.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.900
<i>Don't do it.</i>

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.670
<i>Don't do that kind of thing anymore!</i>

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:38.460
Please answer the questionnaire honestly.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.570
<b>Please write the names of your good friends.</b>

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.570
<b>Tanaka Kanami
Hibino Mayumi</b>

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.010
<i>Good friends, huh?</i>

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:48.100
<i>I've started talking to the library assistant,</i>

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:52.520
<i>but she's kind of weird, 
so I'm not sure we're friends.</i>

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:56.160
<i>She says a lot of annoying things, 
but she's fun to be around.</i>

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.240
<i>I guess we're friends.</i>

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.530
<i>But it would sting if I write her 
name and she doesn't write mine.</i>

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:08.730
<b>Tanaka Kanami
Hibino Mayumi
Mizushima Sa</b>

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:11.820
Time's up.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:12.660
<i>What?</i>

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.050
<i>Wh-What am I going to do?</i>

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:21.390
Enomoto-san?

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.290
Here.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:36.020
We'll never finish putting away the 
returns if you keep reading them.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:39.980
Did you know getting angry 
all the time makes you fat?

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.180
What? You're kidding!

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:41.770
I'm kidding.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.150
Why, you...

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:45.610
Enomoto-san, you're gullible, aren't you?

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:52.300
Th-That's why you're always 
alone in our class!

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.080
There's nothing wrong with being alone.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.290
Oh, really?

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.220
Did you write you have zero
 friends on the questionnaire, then?

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:02.020
You must be lonely.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.610
Not zero.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.590
What? Wh-Who?

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.050
You're the only one I talk to like this.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.490
Well, it's not like it matters.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:28.000
Oh, right. I've got something to do.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:29.320
Bye.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.350
Sayo!

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:37.750
Eno...

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:41.340
Think of something... a plan of some kind.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.960
I don't stand a chance.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.340
Why are you giving up so easily?

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.180
I can't help it.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.090
I won't quit the student council!

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.860
I won't abandon it so irresponsibly again!

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.680
I'll be the vice president until I graduate!

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.940
So... so...

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.800
You're going to be alone 
after school from now on!

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.620
You're going to be lonely!

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:06.290
I can't help that, either.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:11.930
I'll start a movement.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:12.700
What?

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:16.140
I'll start a movement in support 
of romantic relationships.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.760
I'll tell them to save Sayo,

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:22.920
who pretends all she cares about is money, 
but is actually enjoying a healthy relationship.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:23.960
What?

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:27.120
I'll make flyers of you and your
 boyfriend and hand them out.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:31.320
I'll hijack the broadcasting room 
again and tell the whole school.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:33.890
I'll go on the Internet 
and tell the whole world.

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:35.890
Y-You're kidding, right?

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:37.400
Oh, shut up!

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:40.020
You're not going to fight 
for yourself, so I will!

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.120
You idiot!

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.770
Please, tell me you're kidding!

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.860
<i>You're</i> the idiot, Eno.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.560
Excuse me.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.640
Sugihara-sensei, here are 
the forms you requested.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.150
Thanks.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.750
You shouldn't overeat.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:06.980
I'm hungry. I can't help myself.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:11.760
There seems to be some dissatisfaction 
regarding the demotion.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:15.350
Minami, if you're worried about 
something, you can talk to me.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:16.010
What?

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.800
As your former advisor, I'll help you...

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.770
as much as I can.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:25.140
I can always count on you.

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:26.790
Excuse me.

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.090
Sugihara-sensei.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:31.780
I can't believe what Mizushima-san was doing.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:33.900
<i>Sayo-chan?</i>

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.500
The Mizushima from my class did something?

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:39.580
She had been secretly seeing a boy.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:40.790
<i>What?</i>

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:43.250
What? There must be some mistake.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:46.510
A student from the newspaper association 
took a photo of them together.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:49.960
The matter will be handled 
formally in tomorrow's meeting.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:51.670
<i>Nana-chan?</i>

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:56.430
<i>Where did Ichikawa-senpai go?</i>

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.020
<i>Why?</i>

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:03.370
<i>I... I liked her photos...</i>

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:08.270
<i>What am I going to do?</i>

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:12.530
Also, I'll quit the student council.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:13.800
What?

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.920
I'll be taking your camera for a while.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:18.480
You'll need to testify as well.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:19.280
What?!

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:21.860
<i>I didn't mean for this to happen.</i>

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.500
Ichikawa-senpai.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:24.960
Tanahashi-san.

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:27.760
Were you following Mizushima-senpai?

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:28.460
Huh?

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:30.290
Were you pretending to be dimwitted?

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.210
What?

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:36.930
Is it true you took a photo of 
Mizushima-senpai and showed it to a teacher?

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.720
Th-That's...

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:42.040
I used to think you took wonderful pictures.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:43.680
Why would you do this?

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:49.480
I-It's not like that. I... I...

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:56.410
Please don't cry!

00:09:56.410 --> 00:10:01.020
If you cry, I'll... I'll...

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.620
That idiot!

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.180
Nana-chan...

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:12.040
You know, I never really liked her.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.880
What a coincidence. Neither did I.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.380
She's kind of spiteful.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.930
She always hits people where 
it hurts them the most.

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:23.100
She loves money, and she 
always turns up out of nowhere.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.680
And she wears glasses.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:25.970
Yes,

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:30.810
when it comes to what boys like, 
girls with glasses rank rather high.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:32.810
Maybe her glasses have nothing to do with it.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.940
True, Suzu wears glasses as well.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.880
But above all, she's a liar.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.010
That's right.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.360
She lies with a straight face.

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.030
Which means <i>that</i> was...

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:43.660
...also a lie.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:46.200
Why did you make Suzu cry?

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:49.310
S-Senpai, why are you crying?

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:51.920
And Nana-chan, why are you crying?

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:54.810
And Momo-senpai, you're...

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:56.170
not crying.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.380
You can decide who's the 
biggest crybaby later!

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:02.640
Hurry and get inside!

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.590
Operation: Save Mizushima-senpai

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:07.560
Let's get started.

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:09.470
Y-Yeah.

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:13.650
I see, so that's what happened.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.980
I-I'm sorry.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:17.890
It was inevitable.

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:20.860
She's just as much to blame, 
with that sharp tongue of hers.

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:24.900
The official decision is going to 
be made in tomorrow's meeting.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:26.210
But...

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:28.040
The biggest problem is the photo.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.620
It's the most significant evidence.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.790
By the way, what kind of guy was he?

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:37.840
It was dark out, and he was facing the 
other way. I didn't get a good look.

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:40.720
Which means it's hard to see 
anything in the photo, too?

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.590
If we insist it's not Sayo...

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.970
Her glasses are clearly visible.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:46.470
That won't work.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:51.810
I-If we can't see his face, 
could we say she was with a girl?

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.600
He was wearing his uniform. 
That won't work, either.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:59.530
<i>A girl whose face isn't visible...</i>

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:03.490
It's difficult now that Sayo-chan 
has admitted it's her, anyway.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:08.180
Destroying the photo now may 
actually reaffirm their evidence.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:12.640
What we should do is use the evidence.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:15.920
That wig's taking all the intelligence 
out of what you're saying.

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:17.040
What?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:18.640
Ichikawa-san.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:20.050
Y-Yes?

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:22.560
You said you couldn't see his face very well.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:25.430
He didn't have a mohawk, did he?

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:27.880
Why would you do that?

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.560
I could ask you the same!

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.310
Where did you get that wig, anyway?

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.130
I-I suppose...

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:37.730
you could say we were destined to meet.

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:40.140
Don't blush!

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.170
Why do you keep getting more weird stuff?

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:45.780
Forgive me! Forgive me, Riko!

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:53.060
<b>Princess Fuji</b>

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:47.480
Ow!

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:51.720
Don't make weird noises!

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:57.110
This is the true nature of Princess Fuji.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.690
This is the true student council.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:00.920
I think it's nice.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.010
The student council exceeded my expectations.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.490
<b>The Extremely Embarrassed 
Vice President and Secretary</b>

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:08.430
<i>I understand why Sayo-chan 
enjoys this so much.</i>

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:11.150
Please listen to me!

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:14.980
It's part of this important operation.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:16.480
Operation?

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:20.720
Yes. It's <i>his</i> time to shine.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.260
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:30.740
<i>Has she always been so calm?</i>

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:35.230
Mizushima-san will be asked 
to leave the student council.

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:39.500
I will ask you one more time: 
there is no mistake in this photo, yes?

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:43.000
Y-Yes, she was very friendly with him.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.040
He was a very good-looking young man.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.020
What?

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:51.440
Did he look something like this?

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:52.720
Makio?

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:53.390
Who?!

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:07.210
Ichikawa, was this the face you saw?

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:08.970
<b>Wig</b>

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:08.970
<b>Fake Mole</b>

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:08.970
<b>Shoulder Pads</b>

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:11.670
<b>Bound with Fabric</b>

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:14.380
Was he about as tall as her?

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:15.620
<b>Elevator Shoes</b>

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:17.670
Did his voice sound like this?

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:23.090
Nothing could make me happier than 
watching this beautiful sunset with you.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.180
Yes, that's him!

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:26.920
What?

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:29.530
Yes, this is...

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:31.930
The evolved form of Makio!

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.920
<b>Makio Evolved</b>

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.430
He does have a mole.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.540
You're Maki-san, aren't you?

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.770
This is <i>you</i> in the photo?

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:41.650
Yes, that's me.

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:43.710
Th-This is ridiculous!

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.900
You expect me to believe that?!

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.850
There's no way it'll go that well.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:51.360
If you insist on doing it, I'll...

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:56.390
No, I'm the one who bragged about 
having the trust of all the teachers

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:58.870
and put in the effort to achieve that.

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:01.540
Only I can do this.

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:05.380
Why would you lie to protect Mizushima-san?

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:06.680
That's backwards.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.470
She's protecting me.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.060
That's right! She was protecting me, too.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:14.680
Me, too.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.430
Stop this pitiful act!

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:19.680
That's enough.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.270
Senpai may seem cold,

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:28.070
but I know that she's actually very shy and kind.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:33.240
As her advisor, what do you think?

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.940
Tanahashi-san doesn't lie.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:38.040
I had no idea Mizushima-san was like that.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:39.620
<i>You're wrong!</i>

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:42.420
Wait, explain from the beginning!

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:45.340
<i>This is where the real battle begins.</i>

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:48.210
<i>A story of nothing but lies 
would be too ridiculous.</i>

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.670
<i>So we'll mix in some truth.</i>

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:54.260
We found this in the request 
box in the broadcasting room.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:58.700
<i>I'm the one who put that there, so no 
harm will come to any regular students.</i>

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:01.270
<i>I have to shoulder this risk.</i>

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.960
A request for love advice?

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:04.500
To the student council?

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:06.020
What is this?

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:11.280
It's our fault the students misinterpreted 
our afternoon announcement.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:15.020
We know the school forbids 
relationships between boys and girls.

00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:16.100
But...

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:18.310
You know, don't you?

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.700
She'll do anything asked of her.

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.330
Th-That's true...

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:26.250
But, we didn't have contact with any boys.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.640
After much thought, 
she came up with this.

00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:31.940
She would dress as a man 
to understand how men feel!

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:33.430
I'm a perfectionist!

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:38.930
Mizushima-senpai was just playing along.

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:43.850
There's no reason for her to be punished
 so harshly over a single photograph!

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:46.410
Rules are rules. It can't be helped.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:51.860
No one would expect our teachers to be 
so narrow-minded that just talking to a boy

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:53.860
would be a huge problem!

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:57.280
That's why Mizushima-senpai protected us.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:00.990
We didn't expect the teachers 
to accept her testimony

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:03.870
without investigating the matter properly!

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:05.920
It's so cruel!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:12.000
I often run with my ideas on a whim.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.140
Like with that announcement.

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:16.510
It ended up causing trouble for Kurahashi-san.

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:20.600
<i>I assumed it was Kurahashi-san's 
fault then, as well.</i>

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:22.840
The fault is mine.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:27.690
So if Mizushima-senpai is quitting 
the student council, I'll quit too!

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.310
What?!

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.990
Hold on. You guys...

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.680
It's all right, Senpai.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.450
Don't try to take the fall alone.

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:45.300
That's enough.

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:50.000
You're rational enough to know the 
best way out of this situation, right?

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.120
Mizushima-san, huh?

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:55.720
I had no idea she was so innocent.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.700
And she's protecting all those other students.

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.600
That's youth for you.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.180
<b>The Best Way = Endure It in Silence</b>

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:06.290
I understand.

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:09.790
All members of the student council 
will be required to write apologies.

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:11.770
No one will be asked to step down.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:14.530
All right!

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:19.240
Why did you tell such a ridiculous lie?

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:22.280
It'd be easy for them to find 
proof that I have a boyfriend.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.440
They won't find anything.

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:25.760
That's true.

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:27.540
<b>Abandoned her Boyfriend for Six Months</b>

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:30.860
But, your stock values have 
decreased in my eyes.

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:32.500
Especially Maki.

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:34.130
So, what?

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:37.050
Losing a friend would be far worse.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:41.400
In contrast, your value is 
increasing rapidly, Senpai.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:42.280
<b>Actually Cares for Her Friends</b>

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.470
I wish I could sell the lot of you!

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:47.860
I wish you wouldn't 
underestimate my talents.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:50.440
I'll raise my value again in no time.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:53.020
And I never had any 
value in the first place.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.710
It can only go up.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:58.480
I'm not sure what that all means, 
but I'd buy stock in everyone.

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:03.070
<i>Did we go too far?</i>

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.390
<i>Is she so touched, she's crying?</i>

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:14.200
I didn't think there were three 
more idiots just like Eno.

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:24.120
I've never seen anyone like them, either.

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:26.560
Come on, don't forget to thank her.

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:30.370
Thank you very much.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:32.560
Sorry for this bizarre phenomenon.

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:34.580
Thank you, Sensei.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.880
Borrowing the camera must 
have been difficult.

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:38.290
Not really.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:42.280
I would've felt bad for Mizushima and Ichikawa 
if they'd been punished over something so small.

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:46.490
If anything, wasn't it harder 
for you to examine the data?

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:51.670
Sorry, but as her homeroom teacher, 
I'd like to make sure of the situation.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:52.810
I see.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:54.890
I borrowed the camera.

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:56.500
Thank you.

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:57.530
<b>Growl</b>

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:59.670
Have a seaweed lunch.

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:11.520
It reminded me of the chaos 
before a deadline. I enjoyed it.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:14.810
What about your promotion to 
a club and your summer show?

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:20.780
At first, I was thinking of teasing the student 
council a little and getting promoted to a club,

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:23.030
but as long as Nana-chan 
has her confidence back

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:25.720
and we're printing papers together,

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.990
I don't care whether we're a club 
or just an association anymore.

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:33.300
The underground paper 
seems like more fun anyway.

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:36.460
I'm glad the student council is all right.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:38.410
You've got a nasty look on your face.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:40.000
Momo-senpai!

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:43.080
I did it!

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:46.430
I found a real scoop that won't hurt anyone.

00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:47.890
Look at this.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:50.680
Let's print an interesting 
paper with this story!

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.230
Nana-chan, nice work.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:57.480
B-But before that, could 
you help me down from here?

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:00.610
Sensei! Sensei!

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:02.240
What is it, Enomoto-san?

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:05.740
I lied, even though I shouldn't have!

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.770
What?

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:11.640
I erased Mizushima-san's name because 
I didn't think she'd write mine!

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.080
But, I was wrong!

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:15.250
Calm down, okay?

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:18.180
We're actually friends, so...

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.370
Enomoto-san, you're hilarious.

00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:26.110
What are you doing here?

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:29.300
Didn't I say I had something to do?

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.180
My stomach hurts.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:35.350
If you really had something to do, 
don't look so sad when you walk away!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:37.200
I don't know what you mean.

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:51.530
If you answered that questionnaire now, 
I wonder whose name you'd write.

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:53.630
Did you say something?

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.940
Nothing.

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:58.880
Today was exhausting.

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.380
I might as well say it.

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:02.550
Thanks, Eno.

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:11.380
It's fine.

00:22:11.380 --> 00:22:13.750
I got to see something I 
hadn't seen in a long time.

00:22:14.150 --> 00:22:15.430
What are you talking about?

00:22:15.710 --> 00:22:16.930
It's a secret.

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:19.870
What? Come on, tell me. Don't be weird.

00:22:20.050 --> 00:22:21.060
It's a secret.

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:22.060
You really won't tell me?

00:22:22.060 --> 00:22:23.260
It's a secret.

00:23:57.430 --> 00:24:03.230
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:57.780 --> 00:24:00.530
<i>The next episode is the long-awaited 
"teasing Sayo-senpai" party.</i>

00:24:00.530 --> 00:24:02.440
<i>Prepare yourself, Sayo-senpai.</i>

00:24:02.440 --> 00:24:05.130
<i>I'll get you back for all the 
times you messed with me.</i>

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:06.940
<i>Huh? You're calling me 
something different now.</i>

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:10.600
<i>That's because I feel we've 
grown a little closer.</i>

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:12.670
<i>Y-You could've ignored that.</i>

00:24:12.670 --> 00:24:13.630
<i>Oh, what's this?</i>

00:24:13.630 --> 00:24:15.120
<i>You're cute when you're embarrassed!</i>

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:19.890
<i>Um, Enomoto-senpai, would it be 
all right if I called you Eno-senpai?</i>

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:22.570
<i>H-Huh? D-Do whatever you want.</i>

00:24:20.910 --> 00:24:27.010
<b>The Elite Student Council (Photos)</b>

00:24:22.570 --> 00:24:24.840
<i>You stammered. How cute.</i>

00:24:24.840 --> 00:24:26.530
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:24:27.040 --> 00:24:30.160
<b>Don't miss the next episode!</b>
